+<h2 id="common">Common (Human) Constructed Sentences</h2>
+
+<p>Based on the grammar in <a href="common/grammar.md">common/grammar.md</a>.
+Key patterns used: Fossilized Vrykul morphemes (*-garde*, *Tiris-*, *-fal*);
+right-headed compounding (inherited from Titan via Vrykul);
+analytic syntax (hypothetical SVO order, loss of case).
+Common is rendered as English in-game, so <strong>no distinct Common-language
+phrases exist</strong>. All constructions below use fossilized Vrykul morphemes
+and inferred Common patterns.</p>
+
+<table>
+<tr><th>#</th><th>Sentence</th><th>IPA</th><th>Gloss</th><th>Grammar Used</th></tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>C1</td>
+  <td>Strom-garde, Tiris-fal.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈstrɒmɡɑːrd ˈtɪrɪsfɑːl/</td>
+  <td>Stream-enclosure, Tyr-fall.</td>
+  <td>Attested *Stromgarde* (decomposed *Strom* + *-garde*) + attested *Tirisfal* (decomposed *Tiris-* + *-fal*); juxtaposition of two Vrykul-origin place names showing fossilized compounding</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>C2</td>
+  <td>Thor-din, Arath-i.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈθɔːrdɪn əˈrɑːθi/</td>
+  <td>Thunder-[article], Arathi-[suffix].</td>
+  <td>Attested *Thoradin* (decomposed *Thor-* + *-din*) + attested *Arathi*; <strong>speculative</strong> — assumes *-din* parallels Vrykul *-inn* and *-i* is a Common suffix</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>C3</td>
+  <td>Nether-garde, Storm-wind.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈnɛðərɡɑːrd ˈstɔːrmwɪnd/</td>
+  <td>Lower-enclosure, Storm-wind.</td>
+  <td>Attested *Nethergarde* (decomposed *Nether* + *-garde*) + attested *Stormwind*; hybrid structure: Vrykul suffix + Common compound</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>C4</td>
+  <td>Kul Tiras, Bora-lus.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/kʊl ˈtiːrɑːs bɔːˈrɑːləs/</td>
+  <td>[Kul]-Tiras, [Bora]-[place?].</td>
+  <td>Attested *Kul Tiras* + attested *Boralus*; <strong>speculative</strong> — if *Boralus* = *Bora-* + *-lus*, the *-lus* element may be a Common place suffix parallel to *-garde*</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>C5</td>
+  <td>Lordaer-on, Alter-ac.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈlɔːrdərɒn ˈɔːltəræk/</td>
+  <td>[Lord]-[place], [Alter]-[place].</td>
+  <td>Attested *Lordaeron* + attested *Alterac*; <strong>highly speculative</strong> — assumes *-on* and *-ac* are fossilized Common place suffixes, parallel to Vrykul *-heim*, *-garde*</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>C6</td>
+  <td>Arath-or, Strom-garde.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈærɑθɔːr ˈstrɒmɡɑːrd/</td>
+  <td>Arathi-empire, Stream-enclosure.</td>
+  <td>Attested *Arathor* (first empire; decomposed *Arath-* + *-or*) + attested *Stromgarde*; <strong>speculative</strong> — assumes *-or* in *Arathor* is a Common kingdom suffix (cf. *Tirisfal* &rarr; *Arathor* parallel)</td>
+</tr>
+</table>
+
+<div class="warning">
+<strong>Reminder:</strong> None of these sentences appear in any Blizzard source. They are
+constructed to test the internal consistency of the inferred grammatical rules for
+Darnassian, Thalassian, Orcish, Shalassian, Draenei, Zandali, Taur-ahe, Dwarven,
+Titan, Vrykul, Nazja, Tol'vir, Drust, Mogu, Sethrak, Gnomish, and Common.
