+<h2 id="reshii">Investigation: *Reshii* and the *-esh* / *-resh* Root</h2>
+
+<p>The artifact name <strong>Reshii Ribbons</strong> contains the element <span class="inferred">Resh-</span>,
+which may be the full root form of the <span class="inferred">-esh</span> locative suffix.</p>
+
+<h3>The Three Attestations</h3>
+<table>
+<tr><th>Name</th><th>Decomposition</th><th>Element</th></tr>
+<tr><td>*K'aresh*</td><td>*K'ar-* + <span class="inferred">*-esh*</span> or *K'* + <span class="inferred">*-aresh*</span></td><td>*-esh* / *-aresh*</td></tr>
+<tr><td>*Tazavesh*</td><td>*Tazav-* + <span class="inferred">*-esh*</span></td><td>*-esh*</td></tr>
+<tr><td>*Reshii*</td><td><span class="inferred">*Resh-*</span> + *-ii*</td><td>*Resh-*</td></tr>
+</table>
+
+<h3>The *resh* ~ *-esh* ~ *-aresh* Alternation</h3>
+
+<div class="note">
+If *Resh-* is the full root form meaning "realm/world":
+<ul>
+<li><span class="inferred">*Resh-*</span> + *-ii* → *Reshii* = "realms" or "of the realm" (full root form)</li>
+<li><span class="inferred">*-esh*</span> in *Tazavesh* = reduced form of *resh-* with /r/ loss after consonant cluster</li>
+<li><span class="inferred">*-aresh*</span> in *K'aresh* = *-a-* + *resh* = "realm" with linking vowel</li>
+</ul>
+The /r/ loss in *-esh* would be conditioned by post-consonant position, a common sound change
+cross-linguistically.
+<br><br>
+<strong>Confidence: Low&ndash;Moderate.</strong> Phonologically and semantically coherent, but
+the small corpus prevents firm conclusions.
+</div>
+
+<h3>Arguments Against</h3>
+<ul>
+<li>Only three data points; the phonological similarity could be coincidental</li>
+<li>*Reshii* could be a personal name or broker word unrelated to "realm"</li>
+<li>The /r/ loss is unidirectional and not confirmed by other data</li>
+<li>The Ravel connection: *Reshii* Ribbons are associated with the Ravel, whose English name
+means "tangle/unravel" &mdash; *Resh-* could be related to this concept instead</li>
+</ul>
