 <h2 id="wordlist">Comparative Wordlist</h2>
 
+<h3 id="scroll-text">Nerubian Scroll Text: First Attested Sentence</h3>
+
+<p>The only attested nerubian-language text &mdash; writing on a nerubian scroll &mdash; provides
+the <strong>first and only</strong> constructed-language sentence from any of the four "alien" languages:</p>
+
+<blockquote style="font-size:1.1em; margin:1em 2em; font-style:italic;">
+"Unhhh-tikk-a-shisss. Kka shir. Na-l bkah a-shisss. Kreesh kik ik ta. Sohk-a tik hiss a-k-k-k."
+</blockquote>
+
+<div class="note">
+<strong>Key finding:</strong> The scroll text uses <strong>hyphens</strong> to mark grammatical morpheme
+boundaries, while proper names use <strong>apostrophes</strong> for compound boundaries. This dual
+orthographic system is unique among the four alien languages and suggests nerubian writing
+distinguishes between lexical compounding and inflectional morphology.
+</div>
+
+<h4>Orthographic Comparison</h4>
+
+<table>
+<tr><th>Context</th><th>Boundary Marker</th><th>Examples</th></tr>
+<tr><td>Compound names</td><td>Apostrophe (')</td><td>*Anub'azal*, *Ovi'nax*, *Krix'vizk*</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Grammatical morphemes</td><td>Hyphen (-)</td><td>*tikk-a-shisss*, *Na-l*, *Sohk-a*, *a-k-k-k*</td></tr>
+</table>
+
+<h4>Key Observations</h4>
+
+<ol>
+<li><strong>Repeated *-shisss* / *a-shisss*:</strong> The element *-shisss* appears twice, suggesting
+grammatical agreement, parallel structure, or a refrain pattern.</li>
+<li><strong>Sibilant dominance confirmed:</strong> The text is dominated by sibilants (*shisss*, *Kreesh*,
+*hiss*, *shir*), confirming that sibilant-heavy phonology is genuine, not merely a naming convention.</li>
+<li><strong>Linking vowel *-a-*:</strong> The sequences *tikk-a-shisss* and *Sohk-a* suggest a linking
+vowel /a/ that connects morphemes within words &mdash; a feature not visible in proper names.</li>
+<li><strong>Short phrases:</strong> Five short phrases separated by periods; may reflect incantation,
+ritual text, or formal register rather than everyday speech.</li>
+</ol>
+
+<p><strong>Confidence:</strong> Very Low for any specific gloss; High that this is genuine
+nerubian-language text with regular morphological structure.</p>
+
+<h3 id="ar-suffix">The *-ar* Suffix: Nerubian Faction Designation</h3>
+
+<p>The suffix <span class="inferred">*-ar*</span> appears in five nerubian faction/group names and
+one major place name, suggesting it may be a productive collective/faction-designation morpheme
+meaning "brood" or "swarm."</p>
+
+<table>
+<tr><th>Name</th><th>Decomposition</th><th>Context</th><th>Expansion</th></tr>
+<tr><td><em>Anub'ar</em></td><td><span class="inferred">*Anub-*</span> + <span class="inferred">*-ar*</span></td><td>Scourge faction (Dragonblight)</td><td>WotLK</td></tr>
+<tr><td><em>Hath'ar</em></td><td><span class="inferred">*Hath-*</span> + <span class="inferred">*-ar*</span></td><td>Scourge faction (Zul'Drak)</td><td>WotLK</td></tr>
+<tr><td><em>Nerub'ar</em></td><td><span class="inferred">*Nerub-*</span> + <span class="inferred">*-ar*</span></td><td>Scourge faction (Borean Tundra)</td><td>WotLK</td></tr>
+<tr><td><em>Ahn'kahar</em></td><td><span class="inferred">*Ahn-*</span> + <span class="inferred">*-kah-*</span> + <span class="inferred">*-ar*</span></td><td>Scourge faction (Ahn'kahet)</td><td>WotLK</td></tr>
+<tr><td><em>Nerub-ar Palace</em></td><td><span class="inferred">*Nerub-*</span> + <span class="inferred">*-ar*</span></td><td>Queen's seat of power</td><td>TWW</td></tr>
+</table>
+
+<div class="note">
+<strong>Key finding:</strong> If <span class="inferred">*-ar*</span> = "brood/collective" and
+<span class="inferred">*-kahet*</span> = "kingdom," then <em>Ahn'kahar</em> = "Old-kingdom-brood"
+= "the brood of the Old Kingdom" &mdash; with *-kah-* being a truncated form of *-kahet* before
+the *-ar* suffix. The TWW attestation <em>Nerub-ar Palace</em> confirms native (non-Scourge) usage,
+ruling out the hypothesis that *-ar* is merely a Scourge-era designation.
+<br><br>
+<strong>Confidence: Low&ndash;Moderate</strong> for *-ar* as a productive faction suffix.
+</div>
+
+<h3 id="en-prefix">The *En-* Prefix: *En'kilah*</h3>
+
+<p>The WotLK place name <em>En'kilah</em> (Temple City in Borean Tundra) contains the element
+<span class="inferred">*En-*</span>, which would be a third nerubian toponymic prefix alongside
+<span class="inferred">*Azj-*</span> and <span class="inferred">*Ahn-*</span>. However, the
+building's original architects are not definitively identified as nerubian, and *-kilah* strongly
+resembles Arabic *qila* / *kil'a* ("fortress/citadel"), suggesting a possible Blizzard design
+borrowing with no in-universe morphological significance.</p>
+
+<table>
+<tr><th>Prefix</th><th>Attested In</th><th>Inferred Meaning</th><th>Confidence</th></tr>
+<tr class="aqir"><td class="inferred">*Azj-*</td><td>*Azjol-Nerub*, *Azj-Kahet*, *Azj'Aqir*</td><td>deep / realm / domain</td><td class="confidence-mod">Medium&ndash;High</td></tr>
+<tr class="aqir"><td class="inferred">*Ahn-*</td><td>*Ahn'kahet*, *Ahn'qiraj*</td><td>old / ancient / sacred</td><td class="confidence-mod">Low&ndash;Medium</td></tr>
+<tr><td class="inferred">*En-*</td><td>*En'kilah* (?)</td><td class="uncertain">unknown (?)</td><td class="confidence-low">Very Low</td></tr>
+</table>
+
+<p><strong>Confidence: Very Low.</strong> Single attestation with uncertain building origin and
+possible Arabic design borrowing.</p>
+
