 <h2 id="phonology">Phonological Comparison with Nazja</h2>
 
+<h2 id="ar-suffix">The *-ar* Faction Suffix</h2>
+
+<p>The suffix <span class="inferred">*-ar*</span> appears in five nerubian faction/group names and one major
+place name, suggesting a productive collective/faction-designation morpheme meaning "brood" or "swarm."</p>
+
 <table>
+<tr><th>Name</th><th>IPA</th><th>Decomposition</th><th>Context</th></tr>
+<tr><td><em>Anub'ar</em></td><td class="ipa">/ɑˈnʊbɑːr/</td><td><span class="inferred">*Anub-*</span> + <span class="inferred">*-ar*</span></td><td>Scourge faction (Dragonblight) &mdash; WotLK</td></tr>
+<tr><td><em>Hath'ar</em></td><td class="ipa">/ˈhæθɑːr/</td><td><span class="inferred">*Hath-*</span> + <span class="inferred">*-ar*</span></td><td>Scourge faction (Zul'Drak) &mdash; WotLK</td></tr>
+<tr><td><em>Nerub'ar</em></td><td class="ipa">/ˈnɛrʊbɑːr/</td><td><span class="inferred">*Nerub-*</span> + <span class="inferred">*-ar*</span></td><td>Scourge faction (Borean Tundra) &mdash; WotLK</td></tr>
+<tr><td><em>Ahn'kahar</em></td><td class="ipa">/ˈɑːnkɑːhɑːr/</td><td><span class="inferred">*Ahn-*</span> + <span class="inferred">*-kah-*</span> + <span class="inferred">*-ar*</span></td><td>Scourge faction (Ahn'kahet) &mdash; WotLK</td></tr>
+<tr><td><em>Nerub-ar Palace</em></td><td class="ipa">/ˈnɛrʊbɑːr/</td><td><span class="inferred">*Nerub-*</span> + <span class="inferred">*-ar*</span></td><td>Queen's seat of power &mdash; TWW</td></tr>
+</table>
+
+<div class="note">
+<strong>Key finding:</strong> If <span class="inferred">*-ar*</span> = "brood/collective" and
+<span class="inferred">*-kahet*</span> = "kingdom," then <em>Ahn'kahar</em> = "Old-kingdom-brood"
+= "the brood of the Old Kingdom" &mdash; with *-kah-* being a truncated form of *-kahet* before
+the *-ar* suffix. The TWW attestation <em>Nerub-ar Palace</em> confirms native (non-Scourge) usage.
+<strong>Confidence: Low&ndash;Moderate.</strong>
+</div>
+
+<h2 id="en-prefix">The *En-* Prefix: *En'kilah*</h2>
+
+<p>The WotLK place name <em>En'kilah</em> contains the element <span class="inferred">*En-*</span>,
+which would be a third nerubian toponymic prefix alongside <span class="inferred">*Azj-*</span>
+and <span class="inferred">*Ahn-*</span>. However, the building's original architects are not
+definitively identified as nerubian, and *-kilah* strongly resembles Arabic *qila* / *kil'a*
+("fortress/citadel"), suggesting a possible Blizzard design borrowing.</p>
+
+<table>
+<tr><th>Prefix</th><th>Attested In</th><th>Inferred Meaning</th><th>Confidence</th></tr>
+<tr class="shared"><td class="inferred">*Azj-*</td><td>*Azjol-Nerub*, *Azj-Kahet*, *Azj'Aqir*</td><td>deep / realm / domain</td><td>Medium&ndash;High</td></tr>
+<tr class="shared"><td class="inferred">*Ahn-*</td><td>*Ahn'kahet*, *Ahn'qiraj*</td><td>old / ancient / sacred</td><td>Low&ndash;Medium</td></tr>
+<tr><td class="inferred">*En-*</td><td>*En'kilah* (?)</td><td class="uncertain">unknown (?)</td><td>Very Low</td></tr>
+</table>
+
+<p><strong>Confidence: Very Low.</strong> Single attestation with uncertain building origin.</p>
+
