 <h2 id="kobyss">Kobyss Naming (Hallowfall Creatures)</h2>
 
+<p>The kobyss are vicious amphibious creatures native to the Undersea of Khaz Algar, resembling
+large humanoid anglerfish. They attack Arathi settlements whenever Beledar shifts into its Void phase.</p>
+
+<div class="note">
+<strong>Key lore finding:</strong> According to warcraft.wiki.gg, the kobyss are <strong>descended from
+ankoan</strong>, making them <strong>distant relatives of jinyu and murlocs</strong>. If kobyss descend
+from ankoan, their native language (if any) would belong to the <strong>ankoan/jinyu/murloc language
+family</strong>, entirely separate from both the titan-forged family and the Aqir-descended family.
+</div>
+
+<h3>Kobyss Tribal Designations (Common/English)</h3>
+
+<table>
+<tr><th>Tribe</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
+<tr><td>Murkfin</td><td>Murk + fin; inhabits Velhan's Claim islands</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Ragefin</td><td>Rage + fin; attacks Veneration Grounds</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Hungering</td><td>Descriptive; inhabits The Hungering Pool</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Fathomless</td><td>Descriptive; inhabits The Fangs</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Bleak</td><td>Descriptive; inhabits Bleak Sand islands</td></tr>
+</table>
+
+<p>All documented kobyss NPC names are <strong>Common/English descriptors</strong> — there are
+no attested kobyss-language proper names. NPCs include Bristlespine, Droopfin, Sharpfang, Grimslice,
+Kobyss Fighter, Kobyss Trickster, Murkfin Depthstalker, Murkfin Ravager, Murkfin Sciomancer,
+Ragefin Carver, Ragefin Executioner, Ragefin Necromancer, Hungering Necromage, Hungering Shimmerfin,
+Hungering Slicer, Fathomless Ambusher, Fathomless Necromancer, Fathomless Warrior, Darkwater
+Tidecrusher, Bleak Beak-Carver, Bleak Beastbreaker, and others.</p>
+
+<p>The name "kobyss" may derive from Common "abyss" (co-abyss = "of the abyss"), an ankoan loanword,
+or an independent Arathi designation.</p>
+
+<div class="note">
+<strong>Confidence: Very Low</strong> for kobyss-language analysis (no data);
+<strong>Moderate</strong> for ankoan descent classification (wiki-confirmed lore).
+</div>
+
