+<h2 id="kobyss">Kobyss and the Murloc/Jinyu/Ankoan Language Family</h2>
 
 <p>The kobyss are vicious amphibious creatures native to the Undersea of Khaz Algar, resembling
-large humanoid anglerfish. They attack Arathi settlements whenever Beledar shifts into its Void phase.</p>
+large humanoid anglerfish. They attack Arathi settlements whenever Beledar shifts into its Void phase.
+This section documents the full evolutionary chain from murlocs to kobyss and its linguistic implications.</p>
 
+<h3>Evolutionary Chain</h3>
+
 <div class="note">
-<strong>Key lore finding:</strong> According to warcraft.wiki.gg, the kobyss are <strong>descended from
-ankoan</strong>, making them <strong>distant relatives of jinyu and murlocs</strong>. If kobyss descend
-from ankoan, their native language (if any) would belong to the <strong>ankoan/jinyu/murloc language
-family</strong>, entirely separate from both the titan-forged family and the Aqir-descended family.
+<strong>Key lore finding (warcraft.wiki.gg):</strong><br>
+Gorloc (speculated) → <strong>Murloc</strong> (speak Nerglish) → <strong>Jinyu</strong> (evolved by Vale magic) → <strong>Ankoan</strong> (jinyu who left Pandaria) → <strong>Kobyss</strong> (vicious ankoan tribe)<br><br>
+This places kobyss in a language family <strong>entirely separate</strong> from both the titan-forged family and the Aqir-descended family.
 </div>
 
