 <h3>Key Features</h3>
 <ul>
 <li><strong>High /h/ frequency</strong>: 6+ of ~30+ names contain /h/ — unusually high for a WoW language</li>
 <li><strong>Medial apostrophe</strong>: Consistent compound-boundary marking (~25 of ~30+ names)</li>
-<li><strong>Geminate consonants</strong>: *Hannan* (-nn-), *Amarakk* (-kk-), *Fuunid* (-uu- vocalic geminate)</li>
+<li><strong>Geminate consonants and long vowels</strong>: *Hannan* (-nn-), *Amarakk* (-kk-), *Fuunid* (-uu- vocalic geminate), *Ruutani* (-uu- vocalic geminate) — long /uː/ now confirmed by two attestations</li>
 <li><strong>Syllable simplicity</strong>: Predominantly (C)V(C)</li>
 <li><strong>Vowel distribution</strong>: /a/ and /i/ predominate; /o/ and /u/ less common</li>
 <li><strong>Expanded consonant inventory</strong>: New Midnight data adds /ʒ/ (*Zhakir*), /tʃ/ (*Chonon*, *Chua*), /θ/ (*Har'athir*, *Dreth'amar*), /kw/ (*Har'kuai*), /dʒ/ (*Or'jan*)</li>
 <li><strong>Initial clusters</strong>: *Gn-* (*Gnarla*), *Ch-* (*Chonon*, *Chua*), *Zh-* (*Zhakir*), *Dr-* (*Dreth'amar*)</li>

