+<tr class="new"><td>Darkwell</td><td class="ipa">&mdash;</td><td>Corrupted Sunwell</td><td>The Sunwell after L'ura fired a void beam into it. Common-language name. The most significant desecration of the holiest site in Thalassian culture. See <a href="../shath-yar/vocabulary.html">Shath'Yar vocabulary</a> for full analysis</td></tr>
+<tr class="new"><td>Silversun Compact</td><td class="ipa">&mdash;</td><td>Elven faction</td><td>Alliance of Sunreavers and Silver Covenant. Portmanteau of "Silver" (Silver Covenant) + "Sun" (Sunreavers; cf. <span class="inferred">*belore*</span> = "sun"). Common-language compound, not Thalassian, but culturally significant</td></tr>
+<tr class="new"><td>Dawnwell</td><td class="ipa">&mdash;</td><td>Purified Sunwell</td><td>Renamed Sunwell after purification by combined elven heritage. "Dawn" symbolizes the new era of elven unity. No Thalassian form attested; if one existed, it might contain <span class="inferred">*belore*</span> (sun) &mdash; e.g., *Belore'thalas* &mdash; but this is speculative</td></tr>
