alien-comparative.html:763:<tr><td>Xhosa phonological parallels (Hara'ni vs. Zandali)</td><td>Hara'ni &amp; Zandali</td><td>Shared features consistent with proto-troll Xhosa-like substrate: identical five-vowel system /a e i o u/, (C)V(C) syllable preference, high /a/ and /i/ frequency, shared palato-alveolar /&#643;/ /t&#643;/, apostrophe-marked morpheme boundaries. Divergent features: Hara'ni has very high /h/ frequency, geminate consonants, /&#952;/ /&#658;/ (innovations); Zandali has /f/ /v/ /z/, pre-nasalized stops (retentions or innovations). <strong>Confidence: Moderate</strong> that shared accent reflects genuine proto-troll features. Full analysis in <a href="haranir/grammar.md">haranir/grammar.md</a>.</td></tr>
alien-comparative.html:765:<tr><td>*Ka'* prefix coincidence (qiraji &amp; Hara'ni)</td><td>Qiraji &amp; Hara'ni</td><td>*Ka'ark* (qiraji captain) and *Ka'dani* (Hara'ni hunter order) share *Ka'* prefix. Most likely coincidental: languages belong to entirely different families (Aqir-descended vs. elven/troll). <strong>Confidence: Very Low</strong> for genuine connection. See <a href="qiraji/grammar.md">qiraji/grammar.md</a>.</td></tr>
