-as well as proper names of notable tauren figures. The morphemic structure of Taur-ahe remains largely
-speculative; reconstructions are based on compound analysis (e.g., Taur-ahe = "earth" + "speech") but
-should be treated as uncertain.
+<strong>Note on Taur-ahe sources:</strong> Taur-ahe has moderately limited attestation in canon. 18+ confirmed translations and 3 full attested phrases provide more structural data than previously available. The morphemic structure of Taur-ahe remains largely speculative beyond confirmed compounds; reconstructions are based on compound analysis (e.g., An'she = "the Sun", Lo'Gosh = "Ghost Wolf") but decompositions without confirmed translations should be treated as uncertain. IPA for "Taur-ahe" confirmed as /tɔɹ.ˈɑːhɛh/ (TOR AH-heh).
