-
-<h3>Murloc (Nerglish) Phonology</h3>
-
-<p>Murlocs speak <strong>Nerglish</strong> (shared with makrura). Self-designation: <em>gmmmlmrmrgmg</em> or <em>Mmmurlok</em>.
-Names are built from a restricted consonant inventory (/m g r l b k/) with heavy use of syllabic consonants:</p>
-
-<table>
-<tr><th>Name</th><th>Pattern</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
-<tr><td>Brglmurgl</td><td>*Brgl-* + *-murgl*</td><td>Winterfin murloc</td></tr>
-<tr><td>Glrglrglr</td><td>*Glrgl-* + *-rglr*</td><td>Winterfin captive</td></tr>
-<tr><td>Mmmrrrggglll</td><td>*Mmmrrrggg-* + *-lll*</td><td>Grimscale chieftain</td></tr>
-<tr><td>Keymaster Urmgrgl</td><td>*Urmgrgl*</td><td>Winterfin jailor</td></tr>
-<tr><td>Lurgglbr</td><td>*Lurggl-* + *-br*</td><td>Winterfin captive</td></tr>
-</table>
-
-<p>One attested word with translation: <strong>Onoho</strong> = "Deep Shadow" (Razorfin jinyu elder's name for a great beast).</p>
-
-<h3>Jinyu Naming (Post-Evolution)</h3>
-
-<p>Jinyu evolved from murlocs — their naming shows a <strong>dramatic shift</strong> from Nerglish gurgling
-to full CV/CVC syllable structure with complete vowel inventory /a e i o u/.</p>
-
-<table>
-<tr><th>Name</th><th>Pattern</th><th>Role</th></tr>
-<tr><td>Rassharom</td><td>CVC.CV.CVC</td><td>Ancient jinyu Emperor of Pandaria</td></tr>
-<tr><td>Karasshi</td><td>CV.CVC.CV</td><td>Pearlfin warrior</td></tr>
-<tr><td>Izissha</td><td>CV.CVC.CV</td><td>Crane Wing monk</td></tr>
-<tr><td>Lusshan</td><td>CVC.CVC</td><td>Pearlfin leader</td></tr>
-<tr><td>Shushen</td><td>CVC.CVC</td><td>Fallsong waterspeaker</td></tr>
-<tr><td>Fujin</td><td>CVCV</td><td>Pearlfin pearlkeeper</td></tr>
-<tr><td>Sele'na</td><td>CV.CV'.CV</td><td>Unique apostrophe usage among jinyu</td></tr>
-<tr><td>Ot-Temmdo</td><td>CVC.CVCCV</td><td>Pearlfin watersmith</td></tr>
-</table>
-
-<h3>Ankoan Naming</h3>
-
-<p>Ankoan are jinyu who left Pandaria for the deep ocean. Names show continuity but possible simplification:</p>
-
-<table>
-<tr><th>Name</th><th>Pattern</th><th>Role</th></tr>
