-<tr><td>Kotori</td><td>CV.CV.CV</td><td>Hearthstone paladin</td></tr>
-</table>
-
-<h3>Kobyss: Linguistic Regression</h3>
-
-<div class="note">
-<strong>Critical finding:</strong> Kobyss "are capable of speech but only use simple phrases like
-'Animate bones', 'Devour', and 'Violence'" (warcraft.wiki.gg). These are <strong>Common-language
-utterances</strong>, not kobyss-language words. This suggests near-total loss of the ankoan/jinyu language
-— a reversal of the murloc→jinyu evolution. Where the Vale of Eternal Blossoms <em>expanded</em> jinyu
-minds and language, the Undersea and Void energy appear to have <em>contracted</em> kobyss minds and language.
-</div>
-
-<h4>Kobyss Chieftain Names</h4>
-
-<table>
-<tr><th>Name</th><th>Tribe</th><th>Location</th></tr>
-<tr><td>Dreadfang the Merciless</td><td>Darkwater</td><td>Morgaen's Tears</td></tr>
-<tr><td>Grand Gluttony</td><td>Gutter</td><td>Salien Gutters, Azj-Kahet</td></tr>
-<tr><td>Sharpscale the Devourer</td><td>Hungering</td><td>Hungering Pool</td></tr>
-<tr><td>Chieftain Gillcarver</td><td>Sunless</td><td>Sunless Strand</td></tr>
-<tr><td>Lightwalker</td><td>Deepfin (murloc)</td><td>Zul'Aman (surface)</td></tr>
-</table>
-
-<p>All chieftain names are <strong>Common/English compounds or descriptors</strong> — no kobyss-language
-proper names are attested. "Grand Gluttony" is a title, not a personal name. This contrasts sharply
-with ankoan names like <em>Okani</em> and <em>Inowari</em>.</p>
