-<h3>Cross-Family Phonological Comparison</h3>
-
-<table>
-<tr><th>Feature</th><th>Murloc (Nerglish)</th><th>Jinyu</th><th>Ankoan</th><th>Kobyss</th></tr>
-<tr><td>Syllable structure</td><td>Syllabic consonants; mrgl- patterns</td><td>Full CV/CVC</td><td>Full CV/CVC</td><td>English compounds only</td></tr>
-<tr><td>Vowel inventory</td><td>Restricted (mostly /ɜ/, /ʌ/)</td><td>Full /a e i o u/</td><td>Full /a e i o u/</td><td>N/A (no native names)</td></tr>
-<tr><td>Consonant inventory</td><td>/m g r l b k/</td><td>Full including /ʃ/</td><td>Full (smaller sample)</td><td>N/A</td></tr>
-<tr><td>Attested native words</td><td>*gmmmlmrmrgmg*, *Mmmurlok*</td><td>*Onoho* ("Deep Shadow")</td><td>None</td><td>None</td></tr>
-<tr><td>Attested speech</td><td>*Aaaaaughibbrgubugbugrguburgle*</td><td>Full Common dialogue</td><td>Full Common dialogue</td><td>"Animate bones", "Devour", "Violence"</td></tr>
-<tr><td>Proper names</td><td>Gurgling compounds</td><td>Non-English proper names</td><td>Non-English proper names</td><td>English descriptors only</td></tr>
-</table>
-
-<h3>Etymology: "Kobyss"</h3>
-
-<p>Four hypotheses:</p>
-<ol>
-<li><strong>Common "abyss"</strong>: *kobyss* ≈ "co-abyss" / "of the abyss" — Arathi designation</li>
-<li><strong>Ankoan-language</strong>: Could be an ankoan word (*Ko-byss*), but /ks/ in *-byss* doesn't match typical ankoan open-syllable phonotactics</li>
-<li><strong>Nerglish substrate</strong>: *-yss* could reflect gurgling phonology, but *ko-* is atypical of Nerglish</li>
-<li><strong>Independent Arathi</strong>: Unrelated to any known language family</li>
-</ol>
-
-<div class="note">
-<strong>Confidence:</strong><br>
-&bull; <strong>Moderate</strong> for ankoan descent classification (wiki-confirmed lore)<br>
-&bull; <strong>Moderate</strong> for linguistic regression analysis (attested kobyss speech data confirms near-total language loss)<br>
-&bull; <strong>Low</strong> for Nerglish/murloc phonological analysis (limited to proper names)<br>
-&bull; <strong>Very Low</strong> for kobyss etymology (no native kobyss words attested)
-</div>
-
