+<!-- ============================================================ -->
+<h2 id="nerglish">Nerglish (Murloc/Jinyu/Ankoan/Kobyss) Constructed Sentences</h2>
+
+<p>Based on the grammar in <a href="nerglish/grammar.html">nerglish/grammar.md</a>.
+Key patterns used: Murloc gurgling compounding (*mrgl-*, *-murgl*, *-urgl*); jinyu CV/CVC
+syllable structure; *-shi* possible agentive suffix; *Onoho* = "Deep Shadow" (only confirmed
+jinyu word). The Nerglish family is <strong>unique among WoW languages</strong> in spanning both
+linguistic expansion (murloc &rarr; jinyu) and linguistic regression (ankoan &rarr; kobyss).
+No native sentences are attested for any of the four stages. All constructions below use
+attested forms with minimal assumptions.</p>
+
+<h3>Murloc (Nerglish) Constructed Sentences</h3>
+
+<table>
+<tr><th>#</th><th>Sentence</th><th>IPA</th><th>Gloss</th><th>Grammar Used</th></tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Ng1</td>
+  <td>Mrgl-gurg, murgl!</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/mɜrɡəl ɡɜrɡ mɜrɡəl/</td>
+  <td>Gurgling-compound, [exclamation].</td>
+  <td>Attested *mrgl-* and *-gurg* morphemes combined into a two-beat utterance; <strong>speculative</strong> &mdash; no murloc sentences are attested, only the battle cry</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Ng2</td>
+  <td>Aaaaaughibbrgubugbugrguburgle!</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ɑːɡɪbrɡubʊɡbʊrɡubɜrɡəl/</td>
+  <td>(Battle cry.)</td>
+  <td>Attested murloc battle cry; canon form, shown here to illustrate the gurgling phonology that defines Nerglish</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Ng3</td>
+  <td>Gmmmlmrmrgmg, mrgl-murgl.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ɡmɜlmɜrmɜrɡmɪɡ mɜrɡəlˈmɜrɡəl/</td>
+  <td>Murloc-self, gurgling-compound.</td>
+  <td>Attested self-designation *gmmmlmrmrgmg* + attested *mrgl-* and *-murgl* morphemes; <strong>speculative</strong> &mdash; juxtaposes the only two confirmed murloc-language words</td>
+</tr>
+</table>
+
+<h3>Jinyu Constructed Sentences</h3>
+
+<table>
+<tr><th>#</th><th>Sentence</th><th>IPA</th><th>Gloss</th><th>Grammar Used</th></tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Ng4</td>
+  <td>Onoho, Karasshi.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/oˈnoho kɑˈrɑʃi/</td>
+  <td>Deep Shadow, Karasshi.</td>
+  <td>Attested *Onoho* ("Deep Shadow," the only confirmed jinyu word) + attested name *Karasshi*; <strong>speculative</strong> &mdash; juxtaposes the only translated word with a warrior name as vocative</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Ng5</td>
+  <td>Gorai-shi, Lusshan-shi.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ɡoˈrɑɪʃi ˈlʊʃɑnʃi/</td>
+  <td>Gorai-[agent], Lusshan-[agent].</td>
+  <td>Attested names *Gorai* and *Lusshan* + inferred *-shi* agentive suffix; <strong>speculative</strong> &mdash; *-shi* suffix is inferred from 4 names (Karasshi, Izissha, Zusshi, Resshi) but its meaning is unconfirmed</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Ng6</td>
+  <td>Sele'na, Onoho-shi.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/sɛˈlɛnɑ oˈnohoʃi/</td>
+  <td>Sele'na, Deep-Shadow-agent.</td>
+  <td>Attested name *Sele'na* (only jinyu name with apostrophe) + attested *Onoho* + inferred *-shi*; <strong>speculative</strong> &mdash; demonstrates apostrophe compounding alongside the *-shi* suffix</td>
+</tr>
+</table>
+
+<h3>Ankoan Constructed Sentences</h3>
+
+<table>
+<tr><th>#</th><th>Sentence</th><th>IPA</th><th>Gloss</th><th>Grammar Used</th></tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Ng7</td>
+  <td>Okani, Inowari.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/oˈkɑni ɪnoˈwɑri/</td>
+  <td>Okani, Inowari.</td>
+  <td>Attested ankoan names *Okani* (Blademaster) + *Inowari* (Bladesman); juxtaposition of two confirmed CV.CV.CV-pattern names; <strong>speculative</strong> &mdash; no ankoan sentences are attested</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Ng8</td>
+  <td>Ori, Akana, Kotori.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈoɾi ɑˈkɑnɑ koˈtoɾi/</td>
+  <td>Ori, Akana, Kotori.</td>
+  <td>Attested ankoan names; three-way juxtaposition showing consistent CV.CV.CV syllable pattern; <strong>speculative</strong></td>
+</tr>
+</table>
+
+<h3>Kobyss Constructed Sentences</h3>
+
+<p>Kobyss have <strong>no native language</strong>. Their only attested speech consists of three
+Common/English words. The sentences below demonstrate the linguistic regression &mdash;
+kobyss can only articulate violence-related concepts in Common.</p>
+
+<table>
+<tr><th>#</th><th>Sentence</th><th>IPA</th><th>Gloss</th><th>Grammar Used</th></tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Ng9</td>
+  <td>Devour. Violence.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/dɪˈvaʊər ˈvaɪələns/</td>
+  <td>Devour. Violence.</td>
+  <td>Attested kobyss speech; canon forms, shown here to illustrate the near-total language loss &mdash; kobyss retain only Common vocabulary for violent actions</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Ng10</td>
+  <td>Animate bones.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈænɪmeɪt boʊnz/</td>
+  <td>Animate bones.</td>
+  <td>Attested kobyss speech; canon form &mdash; the third and final attested kobyss phrase, all in Common; <strong>no native kobyss sentences exist</strong></td>
+</tr>
+</table>
+
+<div class="warning">
+<strong>Reminder:</strong> None of these sentences appear in any Blizzard source (except the
+attested murloc battle cry and the three kobyss Common phrases, which are canon). They are
+constructed to test the internal consistency of the inferred grammatical rules for
+Darnassian, Thalassian, Orcish, Shalassian, Draenei, Eredun, Zandali, Taur-ahe, Dwarven,
+Titan, Vrykul, Nazja, Tol'vir, Drust, Mogu, Sethrak, Gnomish, Common, Gutterspeak, Shath'Yar,
+Kalimag, Earthen, Nerubian, Qiraji, Ethereal, Hara'ni, and Nerglish.
+Any use of these sentences in fan works or scholarly analysis must clearly mark them as
+non-canon reconstructions.
+</div>
+
