+<h2 id="titan-connection">Titan-Dwarven Linguistic Connection</h2>
+
+<p>Dwarves descend from the Earthen, titan-forged stone beings created by Khaz'goroth. The Dwarven language preserves several morphemes of Titan origin:</p>
+
+<ul>
+<li><strong>Uld-</strong> &mdash; Direct Titan loanword meaning "city" or "facility" (<em>Ulduar</em>, <em>Uldum</em>, <em>Uldaman</em>)</li>
+<li><strong>Khaz</strong> &mdash; Root meaning "forge" or "shape" preserved in both the Titan creator's name (<em>Khaz'goroth</em>) and the Dwarven kingdom (<em>Khaz Modan</em>); three attestations including <em>Khaz Algar</em></li>
+<li><strong>-dun / -den</strong> &mdash; Possible cognate with Titan <em>-den</em> (as in <em>Ra-den</em>); both appear in fortification/authority contexts</li>
+<li><strong>-modan / -dor</strong> &mdash; Possible sound correspondence: Titan <em>-dor</em> (as in <em>Kalimdor</em> = "Land of Eternal Starlight") &rarr; Dwarven <em>-modan</em> ("mountain/kingdom")</li>
+</ul>
+
+<p>See <a href="../titan-forged-comparative.html">titan-forged-comparative.html</a> for full comparative analysis of the titan-forged language family.</p>
+
