 <h1>Shalassian Grammar</h1>
 
 <h2 id="phonology">Phonology</h2>
 
+<p>Shalassian evolved from Darnassian over 10,000 years of isolation under the Nightwell's shield. The phonology shares core features with Darnassian and Thalassian: fluid consonants, vowel-heavy syllables, and melodic intonation <span class="inferred">(inferred from elven language family patterns)</span>. Apostrophes mark morpheme boundaries, consistent with other elven languages (confirmed by Shal'dorei, Shal'Aran).</p>
+
