+
+<p>The five-vowel system <span class="ipa">/a e i o u/</span> is inherited from Darnassian and is consistent across all attested Shalassian names. Vowel distribution appears balanced, unlike Nazja's reduced system.</p>
+
+<h3 id="phonological-patterns">Phonological Patterns</h3>
+
+<ol>
+<li><strong>Syllable structure</strong>: Predominantly (C)V(C), consistent with the elven language family. Attested patterns:
+  <ul>
+    <li>CV: <em>Sha, do, Te, Ar</em></li>
+    <li>CVC: <em>Shal, dor, Aran</em></li>
+    <li>VCV: <em>Elisande, Arluin</em></li>
+    <li>No complex onset clusters are attested in clearly Shalassian words, suggesting Shalassian retained Darnassian's simple onset structure.</li>
