+<tr><td><strong>Mothkeeper Wew'tam</strong></td><td class="ipa">/wɛwˈtæm/</td><td>Mothkeeper</td><td>"Mothkeeper" is a Common-language title (new cultural role); apostrophe compound: <span class="inferred">*Wew'*</span> + <span class="inferred">*-tam*</span></td></tr>
+<tr><td><strong>Yaila</strong></td><td class="ipa">/ˈjaɪlə/</td><td>Tailoring vendor (Female); The Den</td><td>No apostrophe; *-a* ending. Affiliation: Hara'ti. <strong>Confirmed female</strong> — supports *-a* feminine suffix hypothesis</td></tr>
+<tr><td><strong>Yinaa</strong></td><td class="ipa">/ˈjiːnɑː/</td><td>Haranir</td><td>No apostrophe; *-aa* double vowel (long /aː/). Parallels *Fuunid* (*-uu-* = long /uː/), confirming long vowels as a Hara'ni feature</td></tr>
+<tr><td><strong>Yonaa</strong></td><td class="ipa">/joʊˈnɑː/</td><td>Haranir</td><td>No apostrophe; *-aa* double vowel (long /aː/)</td></tr>
