+<h3 id="arathi-name-patterns">Arathi Personal Name Patterns</h3>
+
+<p>The Hallowfall Arathi use a naming convention of [Personal Name] + [Common possessive <em>-'s</em>] + [Common noun], visible in:</p>
+<ul>
+<li><em>Dunelle</em>'s Kindness, <em>Sina</em>'s Yearning, <em>Tanir</em>'s Ascent, <em>Tenvir</em>'s Ascent, <em>Velhan</em>'s Claim</li>
+</ul>
+<p>This is a <strong>Common-language construction</strong> using the English genitive clitic <em>-'s</em>, not an Arathi-language pattern. The personal names (<em>Dunelle</em>, <em>Sina</em>, <em>Tanir</em>, <em>Tenvir</em>, <em>Velhan</em>) may be Arathi given names, but they follow Common phonological patterns (CVCV or CVC structures).</p>
+
+<p>Several Arathi personal names end in <span class="inferred"><em>-el</em></span> or <span class="inferred"><em>-elle</em></span>: <em>Dunelle</em>, <em>Sina</em>, <em>Velhan</em>, <em>Tanir</em>, <em>Tenvir</em>. The <span class="inferred"><em>-el</em></span> / <span class="inferred"><em>-elle</em></span> ending could reflect Elven influence (cf. Thalassian names ending in <em>-el</em> or <em>-il</em>), consistent with the Arathi's mixed human&ndash;high-elf heritage. However, the sample is too small to establish a pattern.</p>
+
