+<h3>Correspondence 5: Palatalization <span class="sound-change">*s &gt; ʃ / _i</span></h3>
+
+<table>
+<thead>
+<tr><th>Proto-Elven</th><th>Darnassian</th><th>Thalassian</th><th>Evidence</th></tr>
+</thead>
+<tbody>
+<tr>
+  <td class="reconstructed">*sindu</td>
+  <td><em>Sindu</em> /ˈsɪndu/ (in <em>Sindu-fallah-nor</em>)</td>
+  <td><em>Shindu</em> /ˈʃɪndu/ (in <em>Shindu fallah na</em>)</td>
+  <td>Initial /s/ &rarr; /ʃ/ before /i/</td>
+</tr>
+</tbody>
+</table>
+
+<p><strong>Inference:</strong> If this correspondence is genuine, it represents a regular
+palatalization sound change in Thalassian: <span class="sound-change">*s &gt; ʃ / _i</span>.
+This is a typologically common change (parallel to English <em>ship</em> vs. German <em>Schiff</em>
+from Proto-Germanic *skip). The palatalization would predict other /s/ &rarr; /ʃ/ alternations
+before front vowels, but no other examples are currently attested. <strong>Confidence: Low–Moderate</strong>
+— based on a single cognate pair.</p>
