+<h3>The *-qiraj* Decomposition: *-qir* + *-azj* — First Aqir Morpheme with Reflexes in All Three Descendant Languages</h3>
+
+<p>The qiraji self-designation morpheme <em>-qiraj</em> in <em>Ahn'qiraj</em> has been
+analyzed as an indivisible root. However, if <em>-qiraj</em> = <span class="inferred">*-qir*</span>
++ <span class="inferred">*-azj*</span>, then <em>Ahn'qiraj</em> = "Old/Sacred [realm of the] Qir"
+&mdash; and the <span class="aqir">*-azj*</span> suffix would be the same Aqir morpheme as
+nerubian <span class="aqir">*Azj-*</span> (prefix) and naga <span class="aqir">*Nazj-*</span>
+(if <em>Nazj-</em> = <em>N-</em> + <em>Azj-</em>).</p>
+
+<table>
+<thead>
+<tr><th>Language</th><th>Morpheme</th><th>Position</th><th>Attestation</th><th>Proposed Meaning</th></tr>
+</thead>
+<tbody>
+<tr class="aqir"><td>Nerubian</td><td class="inferred">*Azj-*</td><td>Prefix</td><td><em>Azj-Kahet</em>, <em>Azjol-Nerub</em></td><td>deep / realm</td></tr>
+<tr class="aqir"><td>Naga</td><td class="inferred">*Nazj-*</td><td>Prefix</td><td><em>Nazjatar</em> (if <em>N-</em> + <em>Azj-</em>)</td><td>hidden realm (?)</td></tr>
+<tr class="aqir"><td>Qiraji</td><td class="inferred">*-azj*</td><td>Suffix</td><td><em>Ahn'qiraj</em> (if <em>-qir-</em> + <em>-azj</em>)</td><td>realm / domain</td></tr>
+</tbody>
+</table>
+
+<p>The phonological identity of <em>-azj</em> in <em>Ahn'qiraj</em> with <em>Azj-</em> in
+nerubian is supported by the final sequence <span class="ipa">/ɑːʒ/</span> shared across all
+three languages:</p>
+
+<table>
+<thead>
+<tr><th>Language</th><th>Morpheme</th><th>IPA</th><th>Context</th></tr>
+</thead>
+<tbody>
+<tr><td>Nerubian</td><td><em>Azj-</em></td><td class="ipa">/ɑːʒ/</td><td>Toponymic prefix</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Qiraji</td><td><em>-qiraj</em> (if <em>-qir</em> + <em>-azj</em>)</td><td class="ipa">/kiˌɹɑːʒ/</td><td>Self-designation in <em>Ahn'qiraj</em></td></tr>
+<tr><td>Naga</td><td><em>Nazj-</em></td><td class="ipa">/nɑːʒ/</td><td>Self-designation/locative</td></tr>
+</tbody>
+</table>
+
+<p>All three share the final sequence <span class="ipa">/ɑːʒ/</span>. This is unlikely to be
+coincidental. If confirmed, <span class="aqir">*Azj-*</span> / <span class="aqir">*-azj*</span>
+would be the <strong>first Aqir morpheme with confirmed reflexes in all three Aqir-descended
+languages</strong> (nerubian, qiraji, naga).</p>
