+<strong>Implications:</strong>
+<ol>
+<li>The dual distribution (prefix in nerubian/naga, suffix in qiraji) parallels the
+<span class="inferred">*tak-*</span> / <span class="inferred">*-tak*</span> distribution
+in nerubian (*Tak'izik* vs. *Aza'tak*). If Aqir morphemes could occupy either position
+with different grammatical functions (prefix = locative, suffix = relational), this would
+be a significant feature of Aqir morphology.</li>
+<li>The qiraji self-designation <em>-qiraj</em> would literally mean "people of the realm"
