+<li><strong>Initial-apostrophe nerubian names as Shath'Yar substrate:</strong> Four nerubian
+    personal names (*Y'tekhi*, *A'zak*, *Ix'lar*, *Ix'zek*) feature initial apostrophes
+    &mdash; a pattern characteristic of Shath'Yar (*N'Zoth*, *N'raqi*, *K'thir*). If these
+    are Shath'Yar loanwords in nerubian, they should correlate with Old God-influenced
+    contexts. The evidence is suggestive: *Y'tekhi* underwent Old Blood ascension;
+    *Ix'zek* and *Ix'lar* have crypt lord associations. However, four names is too few
+    to establish a correlation with confidence.</li>
+
+<li><strong>Nerubian *tak-* element strengthened:</strong> The scroll text element
+    <em>tikk</em> (in <em>Unhhh-tikk-a-shisss</em>) may be a geminated/register variant
+    of the combat element <em>tak-</em>, providing a sixth attestation that bridges combat
+    and ritual contexts. The *tak-*/**-tak* dual distribution (prefix in *Tak'izik*,
+    suffix in *Aza'tak*) parallels *Azj-*/**-azj* and may reflect a systematic Aqir
+    morphological feature.</li>
