+<h2 id="zandali-cognates">Cross-Family Cognate Candidates: Zandali–Elven</h2>
+
+<p>The dark troll → night elf origin (confirmed by <em>The Art of Midnight</em>, pg. 125) establishes a genetic relationship between the troll and elven language families. This section documents potential cognates between Zandali and the elven languages. See also <a href="darnassian/grammar.html">Darnassian grammar</a> Investigation 7 for full analysis.</p>
+
+<table>
+<thead>
+<tr><th>#</th><th>Zandali</th><th>Elven</th><th>Proposed Proto-Form</th><th>Semantic Pair</th><th>Confidence</th><th>Key Problem</th></tr>
+</thead>
+<tbody>
+<tr>
+  <td>1</td>
+  <td><em>-da</em> (kinship suffix)</td>
+  <td><em>-da</em> (kinship suffix)</td>
+  <td class="reconstructed">*-da</td>
+  <td>Father/Mother suffix</td>
+  <td>Low–Moderate</td>
+  <td>Baby-talk convergence possible</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+  <td>2</td>
+  <td><em>Alai</em> "fire/flame"</td>
+  <td><em>alah</em> "light/blessed"</td>
+  <td class="reconstructed">*ala-</td>
+  <td>fire ↔ light</td>
+  <td>Low–Moderate</td>
+  <td>Only root matches; /ala/ could arise independently</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+  <td>3</td>
+  <td><em>na</em> "in/to/of"</td>
+  <td><em>na</em>/<em>no</em> preposition</td>
+  <td class="reconstructed">*na</td>
+  <td>relational preposition</td>
+  <td>Low–Moderate</td>
+  <td>Short CV prepositions universally common</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+  <td>4</td>
+  <td><em>Ma'</em> "mother"</td>
+  <td><em>Min'</em>/<em>Minn'</em> "mother"</td>
+  <td class="reconstructed">*ma~min</td>
+  <td>mother ↔ mother</td>
+  <td>Low</td>
+  <td>Counterexamples show /a/ is shared in other morphemes; not a regular sound change</td>
+</tr>
+</tbody>
+</table>
+
+<p><strong>Overall assessment:</strong> The strongest case for genetic relationship comes from the <strong>convergence of multiple weak signals</strong> rather than any single strong cognate. Three independent morphemes (*-da*, *ala-*, *na*) with Low–Moderate confidence each provide a pattern consistent with deep genetic relationship at ~16,000 years of divergence. The *Ma'/Min'* correspondence is now assessed as likely irregular (not a regular sound change), as counterexamples exist (*na* and *-da* both have /a/ in both families). No single cognate is conclusive, but the accumulation of shared features is more than would be expected by chance alone.</p>
