+<p><strong>Analysis:</strong> Darnassian <em>Aran</em> is now confirmed by four independent place-name attestations
+(<em>Ameth'Aran</em>, <em>Bashal'Aran</em>, <em>Loreth'Aran</em>, <em>Morlos'Aran</em>), all meaning "town/settlement."
+Shalassian <em>Aran</em> in <em>Shal'Aran</em> (Nightborne refuge) and <em>Aran'el</em> confirms the morpheme
+across two elven languages with a consistent semantic core ("dwelling/sanctuary"). The semantic shift from
+"town/settlement" (Darnassian) to "sanctuary/refuge" (Shalassian) is natural: the Nightborne were
+isolated for 10,000 years, during which their word for "town" could narrow to "sanctuary."</p>
 
+<p>The Darnassian <em>-naar</em> suffix (<em>Astranaar</em>, <em>Dolanaar</em>, <em>Sylvanaar</em>) likely represents
+the same morpheme as <em>Aran</em> in allomorphy: both mean "town/settlement" and share the consonants /r/ and /n/.
