+(2) <em>-naar</em> results from sound change /aran/ &rarr; /ɑːnɑr/ &rarr; /nɑr/ in suffix position; (3) distinct morphemes
+with overlapping semantics. Hypothesis 1 is preferred (Low&ndash;Moderate confidence). See Darnassian grammar
+Investigation 8 for full analysis.</p>
+
+<p>The Thalassian <em>-aran</em> in <em>Shorel'aran</em> (farewell) may be a different morpheme
