+<h3>Set 19: Root <span class="cog">*ther-</span> / <span class="cog">*thero-</span> — "beware / battle / strife"</h3>
+
+<table>
+<thead>
+<tr>
+  <th>Proto-Elven</th><th>Darnassian</th><th>Thalassian</th><th>Shalassian</th><th>Nazja</th><th>Gloss</th>
+</tr>
+</thead>
+<tbody>
+<tr class="shared">
+  <td class="reconstructed">*ther-</td>
+  <td>thera (in <em>Tor ilisar'thera'nal</em>, "beware"); <em>Ash'theran</em> (place name)</td><td class="uncertain">(not clearly attested)</td><td class="uncertain">(not attested)</td><td>thero (<em>Ash-thero-sauguine!</em>, <em>Athero bath'rilas!</em>); -tharei (<em>Osh'bala-tharei</em>)</td><td>beware / battle / strife</td>
+</tr>
+</tbody>
+</table>
+
+<p><strong>Analysis:</strong> The <em>ther-/thero-</em> root appears in battle-related contexts across Darnassian
+and Nazja. In Darnassian, <em>thera'nal</em> in <em>Tor ilisar'thera'nal</em> = "beware" (confirmed translation).
+In Nazja, <em>thero</em> appears in three battle cries (<em>Ash-thero-sauguine!</em>, <em>Athero bath'rilas!</em>,
+<em>Osh'bala-tharei</em>), all spoken in combat contexts. The Darnassian place name <em>Ash'theran</em>
+(enclave in Val'sharah) contains the same <em>ther-</em> element with the <em>Ash-</em> prefix also seen in
+<em>Ash karath</em> (command form) and <em>Ash'therod nethanas</em> (untranslated phrase).</p>
+
+<p>The phonological shape is consistent: <em>therV-</em> with dental fricative /θ/, vowel /e/, and
+liquid /r/. The Nazja variants <em>thero</em> and <em>tharei</em> show the expected vowel changes
+under naga phonological development (cf. /e/ &rarr; /a/ in Nazja, as in Darnassian <em>belore</em>
+vs. Nazja's retention of Highborne <em>Azshar-</em>).</p>
+
+<p><strong>Problem:</strong> Darnassian <em>Thero</em> in <em>Thero'shan</em> ("Beloved Student") seems semantically
+incompatible with "beware/battle." This may be a case of homophonous morphemes: <em>ther-</em> "beware/battle"
+vs. <em>thero</em> "beloved." Alternatively, the "beloved" gloss could be a softened derivative of
+"strife/combat" (a student who struggles/strives), but this is speculative.</p>
+
+<p><strong>Confidence: Low&ndash;Moderate</strong> for <em>*ther-</em> as a cross-elven root
+"beware/battle/strife" (Darnassian + Nazja evidence is consistent); <strong>Very Low</strong>
+for connecting <em>Thero</em> "beloved" to the same root.</p>
+
+<h3>Set 20: Morpheme <span class="cog">*-ethil</span> — "diminished / warded / shield"</h3>
+
+<table>
+<thead>
+<tr>
+  <th>Proto-Elven</th><th>Darnassian</th><th>Thalassian</th><th>Shalassian</th><th>Nazja</th><th>Gloss</th>
+</tr>
+</thead>
+<tbody>
+<tr class="shared">
+  <td class="reconstructed">*-ethil</td>
+  <td>-ethil (3 attestations)</td><td>-ethil (1 attestation, shared phrase)</td><td class="uncertain">(not attested)</td><td class="uncertain">(not attested)</td><td>diminished / warded</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+  <td></td>
+  <td><em>Ande'thoras-ethil</em> ("May your troubles be diminished")</td><td><em>Ande'thoras-ethil</em> (shared phrase)</td><td></td><td></td><td>ethil = "diminished"</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+  <td></td>
+  <td><em>Irana'ethil</em> ("Shield against the Shadow")</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>ethil = "ward/shield"? or "that which diminishes [shadow]"</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+  <td></td>
+  <td><em>Ban'ethil</em> (barrow den in Teldrassil)</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>ethil = uncertain</td>
+</tr>
+</tbody>
+</table>
+
+<p><strong>Analysis:</strong> The <em>-ethil</em> element appears in three Darnassian proper names and one
+shared Darnassian&ndash;Thalassian phrase. In <em>Ande'thoras-ethil</em>, <em>ethil</em> is confirmed as
+"diminished/lessened" (the translation "May your troubles be diminished" glosses <em>thoras</em> = "troubles"
+and <em>ethil</em> = "diminished"). In <em>Irana'ethil</em> ("Shield against the Shadow"), <em>-ethil</em>
+could mean "diminished" in the sense of "that which diminishes [the shadow]" &rarr; "shield/ward." This
+is semantically coherent: a shield <em>diminishes</em> the threat it protects against.</p>
+
+<p><em>Ban'ethil</em> (barrow den) is more opaque. If <em>Ban-</em> relates to <em>Bandu</em>
+(imperative "prepare") or <em>Ban'dinoriel</em> ("Gatekeeper"), then <em>Ban'ethil</em> could mean
+"ward of preparation" or "diminished gate" &mdash; a fitting name for a barrow den (a place where
+druids sleep, their consciousness "diminished"). However, this is speculative.</p>
+
+<p>The shared Darnassian&ndash;Thalassian attestation in <em>Ande'thoras-ethil</em> confirms <em>-ethil</em>
+as a Proto-Elven morpheme, not a Darnassian innovation.</p>
+
+<p><strong>Confidence: Moderate</strong> for <em>-ethil</em> as a genuine Darnassian morpheme
+(3 independent attestations with consistent phonological shape); <strong>Low&ndash;Moderate</strong>
+for the semantic analysis "diminished &rarr; warded/shielded."</p>
+
