 <h2 id="kobyss">10. Kobyss and the Murloc/Jinyu/Ankoan Language Family</h2>
 
-<p>The kobyss are vicious amphibious creatures native to the Undersea of Khaz Algar, resembling large humanoid anglerfish. They attack the Arathi settlements whenever Beledar shifts into its Void phase, suggesting a connection to Void energy. The full murloc &rarr; jinyu &rarr; ankoan &rarr; kobyss evolutionary chain and all associated linguistic data have been moved to a dedicated directory: <strong><a href="../nerglish/">nerglish/</a></strong>.</p>
+<p>The kobyss are vicious amphibious creatures native to the Undersea of Khaz Algar, resembling large humanoid anglerfish. They attack the Arathi settlements whenever Beledar shifts into its Void phase, suggesting a connection to Void energy. The full murloc &rarr; jinyu &rarr; ankoan &rarr; kobyss evolutionary chain and all associated linguistic data have been moved to a dedicated directory: <strong><a href="../nerglish/vocabulary.html">nerglish/</a></strong>.</p>
 
 <p>This language family is <strong>entirely separate</strong> from both the titan-forged family and the Aqir-descended family. Key linguistic findings:</p>
 <ul>
 <li>The family shows a <strong>rise and fall</strong> of linguistic complexity: murloc &rarr; jinyu (expansion), jinyu &rarr; ankoan (simplification), ankoan &rarr; kobyss (near-total language loss)</li>

