+<h2 id="pandaren">Pandaren Constructed Sentences</h2>
+
+<p>Based on the grammar in <a href="pandaren/grammar.html">pandaren/grammar.html</a>.
+Key patterns used: *Huojin* = "active way" (inferred *Huo* + *-jin*), *Tushui* = "contemplative way" (inferred *Tu* + *-shui*), *Yu'lon* apostrophe boundary, *-lao* "venerable" (inferred), *Sha* = "negative emotion" (attested as entity name).
+Pandaren has <strong>no attested sentences at all</strong> — the entire corpus consists of proper names and two philosophical faction names. All constructions below are compound juxtapositions.</p>
+
+<table>
+<thead>
+<tr><th>#</th><th>Sentence</th><th>IPA</th><th>Gloss</th><th>Grammar Used</th></tr>
+</thead>
+<tbody>
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Pn1</td>
+  <td>Tushui, Huojin.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈtuːʃwɪ ˈhwɔdʒɪn/</td>
+  <td>Contemplative-path, Active-path.</td>
+  <td>Attested *Tushui* + attested *Huojin*; juxtaposition of the two philosophical factions; both decompose as [element] + *-jin*/*-shui*</td>
+</tr>
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Pn2</td>
+  <td>Yu'lon, Chi-Ji.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/juːˈlɔn ˈtʃiːdʒiː/</td>
+  <td>Jade-Serpent, Red-Crane.</td>
+  <td>Attested *Yu'lon* (apostrophe morpheme boundary) + attested *Chi-Ji* (hyphen-joined compound); juxtaposition of two August Celestial names</td>
+</tr>
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Pn3</td>
+  <td>Shen-zin Su.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ʃɛn zɪn suː/</td>
+  <td>[Shen]-[zin] Su.</td>
+  <td>Attested *Shen-zin Su*; the Wandering Isle turtle &mdash; three-element name with hyphen and space boundaries; internal morpheme boundaries unknown</td>
+</tr>
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Pn4</td>
+  <td>Huo-jin, Tu-shui.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈhwɔdʒɪn ˈtuːʃwɪ/</td>
+  <td>Fire-way, Water-way.</td>
+  <td>Re-decomposition of attested *Huojin* + *Tushui*; <strong>speculative</strong> &mdash; assumes *Huo* = "fire/active" and *Tu* = "water/contemplative" are productive roots combining with *-jin*/*-shui* path suffixes</td>
+</tr>
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Pn5</td>
+  <td>Sha, Xuen.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ʃɑː ʃwɛn/</td>
+  <td>Darkness, Strength.</td>
+  <td>Attested *Sha* (negative emotion entity) + attested *Xuen* (White Tiger, Celestial of Strength); <strong>speculative</strong> &mdash; juxtaposition of negative force and positive celestial</td>
+</tr>
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Pn6</td>
+  <td>Chen-lao.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈtʃɛnlaʊ/</td>
+  <td>Venerable-Chen.</td>
+  <td>Coined compound: attested name *Chen* + inferred *-lao* (venerable); <strong>highly speculative</strong> &mdash; assumes *-lao* is a productive honorific suffix</td>
+</tr>
+</tbody>
+</table>
+
+<!-- ============================================================ -->
+<h2 id="vulpera">Vulpera Constructed Sentences</h2>
+
+<p>Based on the grammar in <a href="vulpera/grammar.html">vulpera/grammar.html</a>.
+Key patterns used: *Vulp-* = "fox" (inferred from ethnonym), *-era* = "people" (inferred), *-a* feminine suffix (speculative).
+Vulpera has <strong>no attested sentences at all</strong> &mdash; the entire corpus consists of five personal names and the ethnonym. All constructions below are compound juxtapositions with extremely speculative morpheme analysis.</p>
+
+<table>
+<thead>
+<tr><th>#</th><th>Sentence</th><th>IPA</th><th>Gloss</th><th>Grammar Used</th></tr>
+</thead>
+<tbody>
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Vp1</td>
+  <td>Vulp-era.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈvʌlpɛrə/</td>
+  <td>Fox-people.</td>
+  <td>Attested ethnonym *Vulpera*; decomposed as *Vulp-* (fox) + *-era* (people); <strong>speculative</strong> &mdash; may be a Common-language exonym resembling Latin *vulpes*</td>
+</tr>
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Vp2</td>
+  <td>Kiro, Nisha.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈkɪroʊ ˈnɪʃə/</td>
+  <td>[Kiro], [Nisha].</td>
+  <td>Attested personal names; juxtaposition of male leader name (*Kiro*, no *-a*) and female name (*Nisha*, with *-a*); <strong>speculative</strong> &mdash; assumes *-a* is a feminine suffix</td>
+</tr>
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Vp3</td>
+  <td>Meera, Serka.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈmɪərə ˈsɛɾkə/</td>
+  <td>[Meera], [Serka].</td>
