 <h4>Candidate C: <em>Aln-</em> &ldquo;deep/source&rdquo; &harr; Proto-Troll-Elven <span class="inferred">*ala-*</span> &ldquo;essence/brightness&rdquo;</h4>
 
 <p>The <span class="inferred">*ala-*</span> root is already identified as a potential Proto-Troll-Elven cognate between Zandali <em>Alai</em> (&ldquo;fire/flame&rdquo;) and elven <em>alah</em> (&ldquo;light/blessed&rdquo;). Hara'ni <em>Aln-</em> could represent <span class="inferred">*ala-*</span> + <em>-n</em> nominalizer, with semantic specialization to &ldquo;hidden/source potency&rdquo; in the subterranean Haranir. The extra <em>-n</em> and semantic gap (&ldquo;deep/source&rdquo; vs. &ldquo;fire/light&rdquo;) make this the weakest candidate.</p>
 
-<p><strong>Confidence: Very Low&ndash;Low</strong> &mdash; see <a href="../darnassian/grammar.html">darnassian/grammar.md</a> Investigation 13, Candidate C.</p>
+<p><strong>Confidence: Very Low&ndash;Low</strong> &mdash; see <a href="../darnassian/grammar.html">Darnassian grammar</a> Investigation 13, Candidate C.</p>
 
 <h4>Candidate D: <em>-mara</em> &ldquo;balance&rdquo; &harr; Zandali <em>-mara</em></h4>
 
 <p>Hara'ni <em>-mara</em> = &ldquo;balance&rdquo; (confirmed in <em>Har'mara</em> = Village of Balance) is phonologically identical to Zandali <em>-mara</em> in <em>Shaol'mara</em> (Zandalari outpost) and <em>Kul'amara</em> (Witherbark chieftain). However, <em>-mara</em> has no confirmed gloss in Zandali, and /mara/ is a common syllable pattern.</p>
 
-<p><strong>Confidence: Very Low</strong> &mdash; see <a href="../darnassian/grammar.html">darnassian/grammar.md</a> Investigation 13, Candidate D.</p>
+<p><strong>Confidence: Very Low</strong> &mdash; see <a href="../darnassian/grammar.html">Darnassian grammar</a> Investigation 13, Candidate D.</p>
 
 <h4>Implications</h4>
 
 <p>If even one of these candidates is confirmed (particularly <em>-nir</em> or <em>Har'/Aran</em>), it would provide the <strong>first linguistic evidence</strong> (as opposed to lore evidence) for the Haranir's descent from the proto-troll/elven population. The strongest path to confirmation is discovering additional cognate pairs that share the proposed /h/ &rarr; ∅ correspondence, which would independently validate the <em>Har'/Aran</em> analysis.</p>

